  "notes": [
    "cgi-io main_exec requires application/x-www-form-urlencoded then session.access(sid, cgi-io, exec, read), then parse_command, canonicalize argv0, session.access(file, cmdline, exec) or session.access(file, exe, exec).",
    "This oracle is bounded to luci-mod-status commands reached via fs.exec_direct → cgi-exec: /bin/dmesg, /usr/sbin/nft, iptables/ip6tables -t glob, iptables-save/ip6tables-save, /etc/init.d/firewall restart. Other commands are HTTP 404 in this slice (lookup_executable is not a live PATH search).",
    "dmesg/nft/iptables-save ACLs are exact cmdlines. iptables/ip6tables list uses a trailing -t * glob. Bare executable fallback is not granted for these commands.",
    "Missing or empty sessionid after a valid content-type is HTTP 403, not 400.",
    "A cgi-io exec read grant without the matching file.exec ACL is HTTP 403 Access to command denied by ACL.",
    "Root list read/write '*' is stock rpcd.config, not a violation (expectation_id root-administration).",
    "Do not emit dispatcher, authorization_violation, path_found, luci object grants, or execv.",
    "shellquote and basename are not sanitizers. canonicalize_path is not a taint sanitizer.",
    "ubus file.exec (rpcd-mod-file) is not staffed, including iptables.js handleCounterReset fs.exec iptables -Z.",
    "The three luci-ssl libexec helpers stay on policy:cgi-exec-file-v1."
  ],
